# shared memory once. All threads then iterate (grid-stride) over the
# spatial output plane (Hout*Wout) for that (n, oc), reading weights from
# shared memory instead of re-issuing global loads for every single output
# pixel. This removes the massive redundant global-memory weight traffic of
# the original one-thread-per-output direct kernel while preserving exact
# conv-transpose semantics (stride/padding/dilation/groups).
